{"ClientSettings":{"Pn":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"P"},"Sc":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"H"},"Qz":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"T"},"Ap":true,"Mute":true,"Lad":"2026-07-07T00:00:00Z","Iotd":0,"Gwb":0,"Tns":0,"Dft":null,"Mvs":0,"Flt":0,"Imp":1,"Tobn":0},"MediaContents":[{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Founded by Greek settlers from Corinth around 734 BCE, the Italian city of Syracuse, on the island of Sicily, grew into one of the ancient Mediterranean's great powers and is now part of a UNESCO World Heritage Site, 'Syracuse and the Rocky Necropolis of Pantalica.' It is forever linked to Archimedes, whose genius still shapes its identity, and to Plato, who came to Syracuse hoping philosophy might shape political life. That layered past still feels tangible at Castello Maniace, a seafront fortress built for Holy Roman Emperor Frederick II in the 13th century, which can still be admired today.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.SyracuseItaly_EN-US3071727282_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.SyracuseItaly_EN-US3071727282_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"A city written in centuries","Title":"Syracuse at sunset, Sicily, Italy","Copyright":"© Balate Dorin/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/37.067122,15.285311/6?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-US&od=2&shading=flat&pp=37.067122,15.285311;S9;Syracuse, Sicily, Italy&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260706_SyracuseItaly\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Syracuse+Sicily&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260706_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260706_SyracuseItaly"},"Ssd":"20260706","Name":"SyracuseItaly","Market":"EN-US","Hash":"3071727282","FullDateString":"Jul 6, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"In southeastern France, on the Valensole Plateau, summer arrives in waves of purple and blue. Valensole—one of the largest plateaus in the region—lies in the Verdon Regional Natural Park between the Durance and Asse valleys, near the Gorges du Verdon and its lakes. From mid-June to early July, depending on altitude and weather, lavender and lavandin bloom and transform the landscape into one of Provence's most recognizable sights. The air carries a sharp, dry, and unmistakably Mediterranean scent.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.LavenderRows_EN-US2831933520_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.LavenderRows_EN-US2831933520_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Sea of purple","Title":"Lavender rows, Plateau de Valensole, Provence, France","Copyright":"© Robert Harding/Shutterstock","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/43.857636,5.974437/6?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-US&od=2&shading=flat&pp=43.857636,5.974437;S9;Plateau de Valensole, Provence, France&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260705_LavenderRows\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Lavandula&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260705_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260705_LavenderRows"},"Ssd":"20260705","Name":"LavenderRows","Market":"EN-US","Hash":"2831933520","FullDateString":"Jul 5, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Today, the United States marks 250 years since the adoption of the Declaration of Independence—a milestone known as the 'semiquincentennial.' This anniversary commemorates 1776, when the Declaration articulated the idea that a nation could be defined by shared principles rather than inherited rule. Two and a half centuries later, this date is marked not only as an anniversary but also as an opportunity to reflect on the nation's long and evolving story.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.LibertyHall_EN-US2562041614_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.LibertyHall_EN-US2562041614_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"The story continues","Title":"Liberty Bell and Independence Hall, Independence National Historical Park, Philadelphia, Pennsylvania","Copyright":"© f11photo/Shutterstock","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"Most of the Declaration's signers did not sign it on July 4, but nearly a month later—primarily on August 2, 1776.","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260704_LibertyHall\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Fourth+of+July&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260704_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260704_LibertyHall"},"Ssd":"20260704","Name":"LibertyHall","Market":"EN-US","Hash":"2562041614","FullDateString":"Jul 4, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"In Okayama Prefecture, when humid air settles over a stream, hotaru—Japan's fireflies—begin signaling. On warm, windless evenings, they often start glowing about two hours after sunset under favorable conditions, inviting silence beside water.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.FirefliesJapan_EN-US2315956275_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.FirefliesJapan_EN-US2315956275_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"The poetry of vanishing light","Title":"Fireflies glowing above a stream, Okayama Prefecture, Japan","Copyright":"© tdub303/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/34.822845,133.813507/7?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-US&od=2&shading=flat&pp=34.822845,133.813507;S9;Okayama Prefecture, Japan&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260703_FirefliesJapan\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=firefly+insect&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260703_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260703_FirefliesJapan"},"Ssd":"20260703","Name":"FirefliesJapan","Market":"EN-US","Hash":"2315956275","FullDateString":"Jul 3, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"At the Temple of Esna, south of Luxor, Egypt, visitors enter a vivid world devoted to Khnum, the ram-headed god believed to have molded humanity from Nile clay. Built mainly during the Ptolemaic and Roman eras, the temple's surviving hall is supported by 24 towering columns, each carved with intricate reliefs and ritual texts honoring various deities.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.TempleEsna_EN-US1999215513_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.TempleEsna_EN-US1999215513_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Inside Esna's sacred universe","Title":"Ceiling of the Temple of Esna, Egypt","Copyright":"© Nick Brundle Photography/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/25.293581,32.556398/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-US&od=2&shading=flat&pp=25.293581,32.556398;S9;Temple of Esna, Egypt&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260702_TempleEsna\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Temple+of+Esna+Egypt&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260702_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260702_TempleEsna"},"Ssd":"20260702","Name":"TempleEsna","Market":"EN-US","Hash":"1999215513","FullDateString":"Jul 2, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"On July 1, Canada celebrates its national day, marking the events of 1867, when the British North America Act (now called the Constitution Act, 1867) united three British colonies into one Dominion.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.DungeonPark_EN-US2499621341_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.DungeonPark_EN-US2499621341_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Canada, carved by the Atlantic","Title":"Dungeon Provincial Park, Newfoundland and Labrador, Canada","Copyright":"© Kaitlyn McLachlan/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/48.666842,-53.084148/7?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-US&od=2&shading=flat&pp=48.666842,-53.084148;S9;Dungeon Provincial Park, Newfoundland and Labrador, Canada&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260701_DungeonPark\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Canada+Day&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260701_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260701_DungeonPark"},"Ssd":"20260701","Name":"DungeonPark","Market":"EN-US","Hash":"2499621341","FullDateString":"Jul 1, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"As the sun sinks low in the Masai Mara National Reserve, the silhouettes of Masai giraffes rise against a blazing sky and open plains. Another day comes to an end in the reserve, which stretches across about 580 square miles in southwestern Kenya, bordering Tanzania's Serengeti National Park. It is a vast expanse, one of the world's greatest wildlife arenas. Rolling grasslands, scattered acacia trees, and the life-giving Mara River set the stage for unforgettable encounters.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.MasaiGiraffe_EN-US2240704874_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.MasaiGiraffe_EN-US2240704874_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Where shadows stretch tall","Title":"Giraffes at sunset in the Masai Mara National Reserve, Kenya","Copyright":"© danm/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/-1.529493,35.170876/8?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-US&od=2&shading=flat&pp=-1.529493,35.170876;S9;Masai Mara National Reserve, Kenya&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260630_MasaiGiraffe\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Masai+Mara+National+Reserve&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260630_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260630_MasaiGiraffe"},"Ssd":"20260630","Name":"MasaiGiraffe","Market":"EN-US","Hash":"2240704874","FullDateString":"Jun 30, 2026"}],"PreloadMediaContents":[{"ImageContent":{"Description":"International Rock Day, observed on July 13, celebrates the geologic building blocks beneath our feet and encourages curiosity about how rocks shape Earth's landscapes and history. From ancient tools to modern mineral uses, these solid structures hold clues to volcanic eruptions, shifting continents, and life over millions of years. Few places display that story as vividly as Antelope Canyon, a narrow slot canyon on Navajo Nation land east of Page, Arizona. Carved from Navajo Sandstone by flash floods and erosion, its smooth, flowing walls reveal how water and sediment sculpt rock over time. Sunlight filters through the canyon's narrow openings, creating beams of light that dance across red and orange stone, shaped by centuries of natural forces. On International Rock Day, landscapes like this turn geology into a living gallery—inviting visitors to see rocks not as static objects, but as evolving records of our planet's dynamic past.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.NavajoSandstone_EN-US9496264383_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.NavajoSandstone_EN-US9496264383_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Born to rock","Title":"Antelope Canyon on the Navajo Nation, east of Page, Arizona","Copyright":"© Mark Skalny/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/40.837774,-118.280526/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-US&od=2&shading=flat&pp=40.837774,-118.280526;S9;Antelope Canyon, Arizona&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260713_NavajoSandstone\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=International+Rock+Day+geology&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260713_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260713_NavajoSandstone"},"Ssd":"20260713","Name":"NavajoSandstone","Market":"EN-US","Hash":"9496264383","FullDateString":"Jul 13, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"If you're looking for Maine at its most untamed, this is it. Katahdin Woods and Waters National Monument stretches across about 87,500 acres of the raw North Woods—where quiet ponds mirror the sky and dense forests seem to swallow sound.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.KatahdinWWNM_EN-US8982810797_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.KatahdinWWNM_EN-US8982810797_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"A wilder side of Maine","Title":"Katahdin Woods and Waters National Monument, Maine","Copyright":"© Cavan Images/Offset/Shutterstock","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/46.156481,-68.717751/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-US&od=2&shading=flat&pp=46.156481,-68.717751;S9;Katahdin Woods and Waters National Monument, Maine&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260712_KatahdinWWNM\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Katahdin+Woods+and+Waters+National+Monument&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260712_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260712_KatahdinWWNM"},"Ssd":"20260712","Name":"KatahdinWWNM","Market":"EN-US","Hash":"8982810797","FullDateString":"Jul 12, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"In France, Port de Saint-Goustan sits just below Auray's upper town, where a small inlet meets the Gulf of Morbihan estuary. The harbor lies at the confluence of the Auray and Loc'h rivers, creating its sheltered, storybook setting. In the 13th century, the Dukes of Brittany built a bridge, a port, and a castle here; the fortress has vanished, but cobbled quays, narrow lanes, and timber-framed houses still line the water. From Place de la République, Rue du Château passes art studios and galleries down to the waterfront; ramps along the Loc'h, built on old fortifications, open views across the port. Cross the four-arched stone bridge to Place Saint-Sauveur, then climb toward Saint-Gildas Church, where the town rises above the harbor. The quay also marks a transatlantic moment: Benjamin Franklin arrived here in 1776, and a dock now bears his name. Today, cafés and small boats fill the scene, while nearby Auray hosts a well-known weekly market and lively summer events.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.AurayBrittany_EN-US7890619884_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.AurayBrittany_EN-US7890619884_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Where Brittany meets the tide","Title":"Port de Saint-Goustan, Auray, Brittany, France","Copyright":"© Rolf E. Staerk/Shutterstock","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/47.664311,-2.977482/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-US&od=2&shading=flat&pp=47.664311,-2.977482;S9;Port de Saint-Goustan, Auray, France&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260711_AurayBrittany\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Auray+Saint-Goustan+France&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260711_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260711_AurayBrittany"},"Ssd":"20260711","Name":"AurayBrittany","Market":"EN-US","Hash":"7890619884","FullDateString":"Jul 11, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Victoria, a southeastern state of Australia, extends along more than 1,000 miles of coastline shaped by the Southern Ocean. From above, its beaches appear as sweeping bands of pale sand edged by turquoise waters and rugged cliffs. This dynamic interaction of land and sea defines much of the region's appeal. The famous Great Ocean Road traces roughly 150 miles of this shoreline, winding past popular surf spots, forested headlands, and seaside towns.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.VictoriaBeach_EN-US7607379912_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.VictoriaBeach_EN-US7607379912_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"The land of moving shorelines","Title":"Aerial view of land and ocean, Victoria, Australia","Copyright":"© Nearmap/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/-36.850086,144.304291/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-US&od=2&shading=flat&pp=-36.850086,144.304291;S9;Victoria, Australia&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260710_VictoriaBeach\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Victoria+Australia&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260710_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260710_VictoriaBeach"},"Ssd":"20260710","Name":"VictoriaBeach","Market":"EN-US","Hash":"7607379912","FullDateString":"Jul 10, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Sunlight cuts through drifting clouds and settles on the terraced slopes of Sapa, where rice fields cascade down the mountainsides like a living staircase. Located in Vietnam's Lào Cai province, this highland region is shaped as much by human hands as by nature. Generations of farmers from local ethnic communities such as the Hmong have carved and maintained these terraces for centuries, guiding water across steep hillsides to sustain each growing season.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.SapaVietnam_EN-US4008171614_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.SapaVietnam_EN-US4008171614_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Tradition in every step","Title":"Rice fields at Sapa, Lào Cai, Vietnam","Copyright":"© Anujak Jaimook/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/22.374456,103.842076/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-US&od=2&shading=flat&pp=22.374456,103.842076;S9;Sapa, Lào Cai, Vietnam&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260709_SapaVietnam\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=L%c3%a0o+Cai+Vietnam&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260709_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260709_SapaVietnam"},"Ssd":"20260709","Name":"SapaVietnam","Market":"EN-US","Hash":"4008171614","FullDateString":"Jul 9, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Set in Guatemala's western highlands, Lake Atitlán fills a vast volcanic caldera. Its deep blue waters are framed by steep crater walls and the cone-shaped volcanoes Atitlán, Tolimán, and San Pedro. Wooden piers stretch into the still lake, emphasizing the contrast between its calm surface and the rugged terrain shaped by volcanic activity.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.LakeAtitlan_EN-US3747076006_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.LakeAtitlan_EN-US3747076006_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Echoes of a volcanic past","Title":"Sunrise at Lake Atitlán, Guatemala","Copyright":"© shayes17/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/14.702858,-91.194628/9?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-US&od=2&shading=flat&pp=14.702858,-91.194628;S9;Lake Atitlán, Sololá, Guatemala&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260708_LakeAtitlan\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Lake+Atitlan+Guatemala&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260708_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260708_LakeAtitlan"},"Ssd":"20260708","Name":"LakeAtitlan","Market":"EN-US","Hash":"3747076006","FullDateString":"Jul 8, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"A bill like a multitool and plumage full of color—the plate-billed mountain toucan is one of the Andes' most distinctive birds. It lives in the hum